@*
    UI-SPEC §11 Queue depth / §12 Rank adjust — shared placeholder shown when an optional
    sibling package (GameKit.Matchmaking, GameKit.Rankings, ...) is not registered.

    LOAD-BEARING (ADMIN-09): tests/GameKit.Admin.Integration.Tests/PanelRenderTests.cs
    asserts the exact rendered substrings "Install GameKit.Matchmaking" (line 47) and
    "Install GameKit.Rankings" (line 59). The body MUST keep the form
      "Install GameKit.{PackageName} and add .Add{PackageName}(…) to your service
       registration to enable {Feature}."
    The wrapper element / class names can change freely. Only the inner text matters.

    Plan 03.1-08 — re-skinned around the load-bearing substring: replaced MudAlert with
    sketch's <div class="alert"> + <div class="alert-heading"> + <div class="alert-body">.
*@
<div class="alert" role="status">
    <div class="alert-heading">@PackageName not installed</div>
    <div class="alert-body">
        Install GameKit.@PackageName and add .Add@(PackageName)(…) to your service registration to enable @Feature.
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// Sibling package short name (e.g. <c>Matchmaking</c>, <c>Rankings</c>). Substituted into
    /// both the heading and the <c>GameKit.{PackageName}</c> install hint.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string PackageName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Feature label that describes what the package enables (e.g.
    /// <c>live queue telemetry</c>, <c>manual rank adjustments</c>). Shown verbatim at the
    /// end of the body copy.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Feature { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
